Third-party code embedded in upstream xEdit
-------------------------------------------

Some upstream units embed third-party code under other terms. These terms apply
only when that specific code is ported. The preferred route is to use an
existing Rust crate instead and not port the unit.

  Core/wbHalfFloat.pas      Neslib.Half, Copyright (c) 2018 Erik van Bilsen,
                            Simplified BSD License (BSD-2-Clause).
  Core/wbMeshOptimize.pas   meshoptimizer 0.21, Copyright (c) 2016-2024 Arseny
                            Kapoulkine, MIT License.
  External/Diff/Diff.pas    TDiff 3.1, Copyright Angus Johnson, freeware with
                            its own conditions (the copyright notice and the
                            terms left unchanged, modifications documented
                            with the modifier's name, free to compile into
                            binaries). Ported in phase 4 as
                            crates/xedit-analysis/src/diff.rs, which carries
                            the notice and the terms unchanged and documents
                            the translation: the view aligns array entries
                            with it, and which entries it pairs among equal
                            alignments decides the conflict status, so a
                            different diff algorithm would not give xEdit's
                            result. The integer compare is the only part
                            ported.
  Core/MSHeap.pas           Windows heap memory manager by Roberto Della
                            Pasqua. Delphi-specific; not ported.
  External/TOM2/TOM2.pas    Generated COM type library import; not ported.

The upstream Delphi submodules (JCL, JVCL, Virtual-TreeView, DWScript, SynEdit,
JsonDataObjects, ImagingLib, FileContainer, vcl-styles-utils,
delphi-detours-library, libdeflate-pas, lz4-delphi) are not ported. Rust crates
replace them. The license of each crate dependency is checked against the
allow list in deny.toml.
